## Quick Reference: Failure Handling Decision Tree

```
Network call failed?
│
├── Is it a transient error (timeout, 503, connection reset)?
│   ├── Is the operation idempotent (or has an idempotency key)?
│   │   └── YES → Retry with exponential backoff + jitter
│   └── NO → Don't retry (or add an idempotency key first)
│
├── Have failures exceeded a threshold?
│   └── YES → Trip the circuit breaker
│       └── Fail fast for all requests
│       └── After cooldown → half-open → test one request
│
├── Is this a critical path?
│   ├── YES → Return error to user (with fast failure via circuit breaker)
│   └── NO → Graceful degradation (serve cached/partial data)
│
└── Is the whole cluster struggling?
    └── YES → Load shedding (reject excess requests with 503)
```

